From: GPT-6.1-Sol <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: q6afe: correlate LPASS votes and confirm devotes

Complete audit F5 and the local 0063 transaction contract. Use a dedicated
IRQ-safe reply state, opaque never-reused APR generation tokens, exact
payload validation and nonzero handles. Stale/opcode-mismatched replies
cannot wake another request. Invalidate timed-out tokens under the same
lock as callbacks. Devotes now wait for DSP acknowledgement. Keep desired,
confirmed and uncertain state per block; failed vote/devote blocks reuse
until the AFE service is rebound after DSP restart. CCF unprepare cannot
return errors, so retain and report uncertainty rather than invent success.

No matching upstream backport found in lore/kernel.org searches. APR token
is opaque; block id remains in the request payload. Stock firmware echo of
the full token and devote acknowledgement need hardware qualification.
Hardware: idle/capture cycles, all LPASS blocks, reordered/truncated/zero-
handle replies, same-block timeout/retry, and ADSP service rebind.

